# Network

- All HTTP goes through `ApiClient` + the shared `Dio` from `DioClientSetup`. Do not construct a feature-local `Dio()`.
- Endpoints: `AppEndpoints` only. Feature Api classes call `get/post/put/delete` and parse JSON. No mapping, no business rules.
- Return `Result<T>`. `ApiClient` already wraps failures via `ErrorMapper`.

Retry (`executeWithRetry()` on the shared client/repository helper — add it once in `core/network/` if missing, never per-call):

| Method | Auto-retry |
|---|---|
| GET | yes, via `executeWithRetry()` |
| PUT | only if the server contract is confirmed idempotent |
| POST / DELETE | never, unless an idempotency key is explicit |

```dart
// BAD — POST retried in a loop
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) { await api.createCourse(body); }

// GOOD
await executeWithRetry(() => api.getCourses());
await api.createCourse(body); // once
```

CancelToken is required for upload, download, pagination, and search-as-you-type. Release on controller dispose: Riverpod `ref.onDispose()`, BLoC `close()`. Stale in-flight results must not land in state.

Government/military hosts: certificate pinning in `lib/core/network/` is a blocker, not a follow-up. No pinning → the Data layer is not done.
